          "facts": "The petitioner, a Mauritius company, held 3.48% in Devas Multimedia Pvt. Ltd. On 28 January 2005, Devas and Antrix Corporation entered into an agreement for lease of space-segment capacity on ISRO/Antrix S-band spacecraft. Antrix terminated the agreement in 2011. Devas pursued ICC arbitration and obtained an award for USD 562.5 million. These facts are recorded in the uploaded ASIM account, printed pp. 108–109.\n\nOn 14 January 2021, Antrix’s Chairman-cum-Managing Director sent the Ministry of Corporate Affairs a detailed request for authority to seek winding up, setting out the transaction and allegations. Central Government authorisation followed on 18 January 2021. Antrix petitioned the NCLT; admission and provisional-liquidator orders were made, and the shareholder pursued the NCLAT route and an application to participate before NCLT. The writ sought to challenge the statutory authorisation route and undo the authorisation and resulting proceedings. 2",
          "issues": "Whether ground for just and equitable winding up or substratum failure is made out.",
