          "facts": "Madras Bar Association challenged the constitutional validity of Chapter XXVII (Sections 407–434) of the Companies Act, 2013 establishing the National Company Law Tribunal (NCLT) and National Company Law Appellate Tribunal (NCLAT). The challenge attacked the transfer of company jurisdiction from High Courts to tribunals, executive dominance in the selection committee, and the eligibility qualifications for technical members.",
