          "ratio": "A.K. Sikri J. for the 5-Judge Constitution Bench held that Parliament possesses legislative competence to establish specialist company tribunals. However, tribunalisation must satisfy judicial independence and separation of powers: (1) The selection committee cannot be executive-dominated and must be headed by the Chief Justice of India or nominee with a casting vote, (2) Technical members must possess specialized expertise and cannot sit without judicial members, and (3) Provisions allowing joint-secretaries as technical members violated judicial independence and were struck down.",
