          "ratio": "=\"#section-432\">432433434Source-conscious by design.\nDU extracts first. Full-judgment additions marked. Reported PYQs distinguished from original practice.\n\nLegal time matters.\nPrescribed holdings and later amendments are kept separate.\n\nPrepared 08 September 2026\nSelf-contained · Offline-readyUniversity of Delhi · LL.B. · LB-303 · Topic 09\n\nAdjudicatory\nBodies.\nNCLT & NCLAT: the architecture of specialist justice. A DU-first guide to independent design, fair procedure and the limits of jurisdiction.\n\n407–434Including section 417A02Deep case dossiers18Structured chapters22,729Words of study materialConstitution & selectionMBA · 2015Embassy · 2019PYQs & answersLater-law appendix\n\n01 · How to study this topic\n\nA tribunal must be independent enough to adjudicate, but it must also remain within the jurisdiction Parliament has given it. These are the two organising ideas of DU Topic 9.\n\nThis guide follows the prescribed syllabus: National Company Law Tribunal (NCLT) and National Company Law Appel",
