          "issues": "Key legal questions examined and determined by the Court in Union of India v. West Coast Paper Mills Ltd..",
          "arguments": "• The cause of action arose on the Tribunal's declaration (18-4-1966); under Art. 58 the three-year clock then began; suits of 1973–74 were 4–5 years late.\n\n • No stay of the Tribunal's judgment was ever granted by the SC — the interim order was only partial — so the judgment was operative and enforceable, and pendency of the SLP could not exclude time.\n\n • Under s. 46A, Indian Railways Act, the Tribunal's judgment was final; the refund claim stood on it and could not be deferred.\n\n • Reliance: Juscurn Boid (PC), Maqbul Ahmad (PC), P.K. Kutty (SC), Mohinder Singh Jagdev (SC) — \"once limitation starts running, it runs its full course\".",
