          "issues": "Key legal questions examined and determined by the Court in The Commissioner of Sales Tax, U.P. v. M/s. Madan Lal Das & Sons, Bareilly.",
          "arguments": "• The U.P. Sales Tax Act is a complete code prescribing its own limitation for revisions; the Limitation Act's s.12(2) has no room.\n\n • The rules did not require a copy of the order to be filed with the revision petition — so no time for obtaining it could be \"requisite\".\n\n • A copy had already been served on the dealer under the Act; the loss was his own — the fresh copy was a luxury, not a requisite.",
