          "arguments": "• s.18 revival: the respondents, in the registered deed of 11-1-1960, acknowledged the mortgage; a fresh period should run from that date, making the 1980 suit timely.\n\n • Inder Singh line: for an unregistered mortgage, possession perfects a valid mortgage only after 12 years — limitation (60 years) could not start before 1905; the acknowledgment of 1960 fell within the live period.\n\n • Approbate-reprobate (C. Beepathuma, AIR 1965 SC 241): the respondents took the benefit of the mortgage under the deed — they cannot deny the mortgagors' corresponding right to redeem.\n\n • The Redemption of Mortgages (Punjab) Act, 1913 first gave a redemption procedure — limitation for redemption could not run before 1913.\n\n • Under Art. 61(a), the right to redeem accrues only when the mortgagor tenders the amount or the mortgagee communicates satisfaction — neither had happened, so time never began.",
