          "modelAnswer": "Model Answer\n **The DU solved-papers book answers both questions by cross-reference to Q.1/2019 (answered in full above)** — the complete response on the doctrine (meaning, maxims, public policy, conditions, non-exhaustiveness) is there; the co-defendants head stands on these authorities: the three conditions (*Iftikhar Ahmed*, AIR 1974 SC 749 — the prescribed case; restated in *Union of India v. S. Narasimhulu Naidu* (2021 SC)); binding effect even on dismissal of the earlier suit (*Munni Bibi*, AIR 1931 PC 114); the notice qualification for non-contesting parties (*Chandu Lal*, AIR 1950 PC 17); non-application to proforma defendants; and the writ-side analogue — pleas available but not raised in a writ are constructively barred (*Nawab Hussain*, AIR 1977 SC 1680). For a 4–5 mark answer, structure: (1) s. 11 basics; (2) the three conditions; (3) illustration (A v. B & C); (4) Iftikhar Ahmed facts in five lines; (5) the PC refinements."
