          "unit": "Reference, Review, Revision & Inherent Powers",
          "file": "sem 3/cpc/CPC_Topics_7-8_Reference_Revision_Review_Inherent_Powers.html",
          "anchorId": "pyq-u3-6",
          "question": "EXPECTED Q: “Subsequent Supreme Court decision overrules law on which decree based — review?” [3 marks]",
          "modelAnswer": "**No.** **Explanation to O.47 R.1 (1976)**: subsequent reversal/modification by superior court in another case = **not ground**. Review needs **discovery/patent error/analogous reason existing at decree time**. Remedy = **appeal/review to superior court, or retrospective legislation** (which IS analogous ground). Cite *Haridas Das para 10*.\n\n### 8. Appendix — 1-Day Revision Kit BARE-ACT RECKONER • MNEMONICS • LAST-NIGHT CHECKLIST\n\n### 8.1 Bare-Act Ready Reckoner (memorise italicised words)\n\nProvisionOne-line core (verbatim phrases bold)\n**S.113 + Proviso****May** state & refer for HC opinion; **SHALL** refer if **validity** question **necessary**, thinks **invalid/inoperative**, **not so declared** by HC/SC.\n**O.46 R.1–5****No-appeal** suit/appeal/execution + **reasonable doubt** + **statement + own opinion**; **stay/contingent, no execution**; HC **decide/transmit; alter/cancel/quash**; costs in cause.\n**S.114 (a)(b)(c)****Appeal allowed but not preferred / no appeal allowed / Small Cause reference** → same court, **as it thinks fit**.\n**O.47 R.1****Discovery despite diligence / error apparent / other sufficient reason**; R.1(2) other-party appeal; **Explanation: subsequent overruling ≠ ground**.\n**O.47 Rr.4–9****Reject if no ground; grant after notice + strict proof; same Judge; equally divided = reject; rejection not appealable, grant appealable; restoration; register + rehear; NO second review.**\n**S.115 (1)(a)(b)(c)****Case decided + subordinate + no appeal** + **(a) excess / (b) failure / (c) illegal-irregular** → as it thinks fit.\n**S.115 Proviso+(2)+(3)+Exp.****Proviso: interlocutory only if favour → finally disposed**; (2) **appeal lies → no revision**; (3) **no auto-stay**; Exp: **case decided includes orders/issues**.\n**S.151****Nothing shall limit inherent power** for **ends of justice / prevent abuse**. **Saved, not conferred; complementary; procedural-only; exceptional.**\n**Ss.148/149**148: **enlarge Court-fixed period even after expiry** (≤30 days); 149: **deficit fee at any stage, retrospective**.\n\n### 8.2 Mnemonics\n\n• **Review grounds — “D-E-S” (DESperate):** **D**iscovery, **E**rror apparent, **S**ufficient reason (analogous). Explanation = “**Subsequent ≠ Sufficient**.”\n\n• **Revision conditions — “C-S-N-J” (CaSeNJi):** **C**ase decided, **S**ubordinate, **N**o appeal, **J**urisdictional error. Proviso = “**Favour → Finally disposed?**”\n\n• **Reference — “P-Q-R-O”:** **P**ending, **Q**uestion of law/vires, **R**easonable doubt/prima facie invalid, **O**pinion + statement.\n\n• **S.151 — “E-A-C-P-E”:** **E**nds, **A**buse, **C**omplementary (not controlled), **P**rocedural-only, **E**xceptional.\n\n• **Second review — “R.9 = No Round 2”.** Revision stay — “**115(3): file ≠ stay**.”\n\n### 8.3 Last-Night Checklist (tick before exam)\n\n• ☐ Can reproduce **S.113 proviso (SHALL), O.47 R.1 grounds + Explanation, S.115 proviso + (2)(3), S.151** verbatim?\n\n• ☐ Can draw **Reference / Review-3-stages / Revision-Q1–Q6 / S.151 tree** from memory?\n\n• ☐ Can write **6-row distinction table + second-review paragraph** in 12 minutes?\n\n• ☐ Can summarise **Haridas Das (O.2 R.2 irrelevant + leave reserved + 4 precedents)** in 8 lines?\n\n• ☐ Can summarise **Mahant Ram Dass (peremptory in terrorem + Ss.148/149/151 + 2 months)** in 8 lines?\n\n• ☐ Can state **Manohar Lal twin ratio (power YES, exercise NO on facts + Cohen/Hyman)** in 6 lines?\n\n• ☐ Remember **costs-personal (Sherlekar), refusal revisable (Phulchand), no suo motu review, revision suo motu YES, 30-day review / 90-day revision limitation**?\n\n#### 📖 SOURCES CITED (FOR EXAMINER CONFIDENCE — WRITE 1 LINE IN ANSWER)\n\n*DU LB-302 (2025) pp.50–57 (Haridas Das; Mahant Ram Dass), pp.121–127 (Manohar Lal); CPC Bare Act Ss.113,114,115,148–153, O.46, O.47; Universal Law Series (Reference/Review/Revision/Inherent Q&A, Ram Chand, Surinder Singh); Takwani Chs.7–9, Inherent Powers; PYQ Solved Papers Q.2(b)/2019, Q.4(a)/2017, Q.6(b)/2018, Q.4/2019.* Answers above synthesise these; bare-act quotes verified against the_code_of_civil_procedure,_1908 (workspace).\n\nDU LL.B LB-302 • Topics 7 & 8 Master Notes • Reference (S.113) • Review (S.114/O.47) • Revision (S.115) • Inherent Powers (S.151) • Based primarily on DU case material + Bare Act + Universal + Takwani + PYQ till 2023 • For study use • 9 Sept 2026\n🖨️ Print / Save PDF"
