          "modelAnswer": "### ★ MODEL COMMENT (10-mark essay)\n\n**Thesis:** Restates **O.6 R.17 + Kisandas twin tests + Jai Jai Ram/Purushottam/Amulakchand rule** (DU Jai Jai Ram para 6: *“all amendments as necessary for real Q unless injustice”*).\n\n**Elaboration (6m):** Handmaid/Cooper/Cropper object; **negligence/lateness immaterial if costs cure (Clarpede)**; **at any stage incl. appeal/SC/execution** subject to **2002 proviso diligence**; **A.K. Gupta doctrine** (new claim/new facts/new ideas vs additional approach; Charan/Leach even after limitation where substance pleaded); **Ganesh bundle + curable unless ab initio absent / newly-constituted time-barred**; **Dalip 9 checklist**; **WS liberal + alternative unless admission withdrawn (BK Pillai/Heeralal)**.\n\n**Limits (3m):** Mulla/Takwani 4–5: unnecessary, **wholly displacing (Steward/Pollock)**, **accrued right (Weldon; Charan Das special-circumstances exception)**, **new/inconsistent/mala fide**; **Ganga Bai care**; procedure (hear, reasons, costs, R.18).\n\n**Conclusion (1m):** Rule balances **merits/multiplicity-avoidance vs fairness/accrued rights**; Dalip/BK Pillai show courts **prefer same-lis costs-cured adjudication over fresh suits**."
