          "question": "PYQ 3 — Q.2(a)/2018: Ghasita Ram does business as “Ghasita Ram & Sons”, sues X in firm name. X: unregistered, cannot sue. Ghasita Ram seeks to amend to own name. Allow? At what stage? With case laws.",
          "modelAnswer": "### ★ MODEL ANSWER\n\n**Yes, allow at any stage (trial/appellate) on costs — *Jai Jai Ram (1969)* directly governs.** Business-name suit by real proprietor = **misdescription of existing person, not non-existent nullity** (*Amulakchand/Beaumont*); plaintiff competent as **individual/HUF manager**; **no bona fide-averment requirement**; amendment **relates back to institution → no limitation** (not S.21 new party). *Purushottam* (O.30 enabling, outside-India analogy) supports. *Ganesh* (capacity clarification) + *Mohan Singh/Ippili* (no prejudice) reinforce. **Stage:** O.6 R.17 **at any stage** (trial, first/second appeal, revision, SC); post-trial proviso satisfied — **prompt on objection, diligence, no new matter** (Q.3/2020). Impose **costs + consequential amendment** to WS. Only refuse if **mala fide or truly non-existent plaintiff** (not here)."
