          "anchorId": "pyq-u4-4",
          "question": "PYQ 4 — Q.3/2020 OBE (25m): X+Y partners in unregistered ABC & Co. Firm to recover Rs.1,00,000 from Z. X sues in firm name. Z: partners not impleaded. X+Y seek to add names. What if after commencement of trial? Statutory provisions + case law.",
          "modelAnswer": "### ★ MODEL ANSWER (25-mark OBE — expanded)\n\n**Issues:** (1) Unregistered-firm bar (S.69 Partnership + O.30)? (2) **O.1 R.10 (add plaintiffs, bona fide + necessary, consent)** + **O.6 R.17 (misdescription)**? (3) **Limitation — S.21 relation-back vs Jai Jai Ram relation-back**? (4) **Post-trial proviso diligence**?\n\n**Law (10m):** Quote **O.6 R.17 + proviso + O.1 R.10(1)(2) + S.21(1) proviso**. *Jai Jai Ram:* firm/business-name by real persons = **misdescription → amend + relate back to filing, no S.21 new-suit limitation**; **no bona fide-averment rule** (but bona fide present here — prompt). *Ganesh:* capacity/dissolution clarification = **same cause, notice only**; *A.K. Gupta:* **additional approach vs new ideas**; *Karuppaswamy/Ram Prasad:* **S.21 proviso bona fide → relate back** even for added parties. *Rajesh Aggarwal/South Konkan/Van Vibhag:* **proviso diligence + liberal if irreparable loss**.\n\n**Application (10m):** X+Y are **real partners, existing persons**; firm name = **compendious/misdescription** (*Purushottam*); adding names **does not substitute cause (same Rs.1L debt, same contract)**, only **proper description for real Q**; Z’s **S.69/O.30 objection cured**; **no accrued limitation right taken** (debt suit in time; substance pleaded). **Even after trial:** allow — **diligence shown (moved on Z’s preliminary objection)**, matter **could not have been raised earlier in proper form before objection** (or was already in substance), **no surprise/prejudice beyond costs**. Court records **diligence finding + costs + amended plaint service + additional WS opportunity**. Refuse only if **mala fide/deliberate concealment + lapsed-right prejudice** (absent).\n\n**Decision (5m):** *“Leave always granted unless mala fide or irreparable injury beyond costs → allow.”* **Allow addition/amendment, relate back, costs to Z, proceed on merits.** Distinguish *Steward/Weldon/Heeralal* (displacing/new-barred/withdrawal — inapplicable)."
