          "anchorId": "pyq-u4-6",
          "question": "EXPECTED — Short notes (5m each): (a) Misdescription vs non-existent (b) Proviso to O.6 R.17 (c) Pollock test (d) S.21 + O.1 R.10",
          "modelAnswer": "**(a)** *Jai Jai Ram/Amulakchand/Purushottam:* misdescription = existing person wrongly described → **amend + costs + relate back**; non-existent = no person → **nullity, no cure**. Firm/HUF names usually former.\n\n**(b)** 2002 proviso: **post-commencement bar unless due diligence**; trial = issues + evidence; *Van Vibhag* (11-yr delay refused) vs *South Konkan* (liberal if irreparable). Record **diligence finding**.\n\n**(c)** *Steward;* Pollock: **recoupable by costs/otherwise?** Wholly displaced → refuse. Used in tenant + tramway answers.\n\n**(d)** R.10 adds (any stage, consent, amend+serve); S.21(1) **deemed from addition**; proviso **bona fide → relate back** (*Karuppaswamy*); (2) **assignment/devolution/transposition/purchaser exceptions**.\n\n### 6. Appendix — 1-Day Revision Kit RECKONER • MNEMONICS • CHECKLIST\n\n### 6.1 Bare-Act Reckoner (memorise bold)\n\nProvisionCore\n**O.1 R.1/R.3****Same act/transaction/series + common Q law/fact** (joint/several/alternative); **“and” cumulative**; object **multiplicity**.\n**O.1 Rr.2/3A/4–7****Separate trial if embarrass/delay**; judgment for/against some **without amendment**; R.5 **not all relief**; R.6 **one-contract option**; R.7 **doubt → join**.\n**Necessary v Proper**Necessary: **relief + effective impossible**; Proper: **effective possible, complete needs**. Tests: *Hardeva/Kasturi*.\n**O.1 R.9 + proviso****No defeat by mis/non-joinder; deal with parties before court — EXCEPT necessary-non-joinder.**\n**O.1 R.10****Wrong plaintiff (bona fide + necessary); strike/add (ought/necessary); consent for plaintiff; amend+serve; S.21 deeming.**\n**O.1 R.13****Earliest / before issues, else waived** (unless subsequently arose).\n**O.6 R.17 + proviso****At any stage, just terms, real Q — post-trial only if due diligence.** Handmaid; **Kisandas (necessary + without injustice)**.\n**O.6 R.18****Time/14 days or lapse** (extendable).\n**S.21 Limitation****Added = from addition; bona fide → relate back; assignment/devolution/transposition excepted.**\n\n### 6.2 Mnemonics\n\n• **Joinder — “SAC”:** **S**ame transaction + **A**nd + **C**ommon Q. R.9 — **“Mis/Proper = Proceed; Necessary = Perish.”** R.10 — **“BANS”:** **B**ona fide, **A**dd/strike, **N**ecessary for complete, **S**erve amended.\n\n• **Amend allow — “NADI”:** **N**ecessary for real Q, **A**dditional approach (not new ideas), **D**iligence (post-trial), **I**njustice-free (costs cure). Refuse — **“WINDM”:** **W**holly displaces, **I**nconsistent/destructive, **N**ew time-barred, **D**ishonest (mala fide), **M**eritless-technical (unnecessary).\n\n• **Dalip 9 — “NABI PDTEN”:** **N**ecessary, **A**lter-cause no, **B**ar inconsistent, **I**njustice compensable, **P**re-time-bar no, **D**efeat-right no, **T**echnicality no suffering, **E**xtra delay→costs, **N**on-fraud error allow.\n\n• **Cases — “JGDB”:** **J**ai (misdescription), **G**anesh (bundle/capacity), **D**alip (9 rules), **B**K (WS alternative).\n\n### 6.3 Last-Night Checklist\n\n• ☐ Quote **R.1/R.3 twins, R.9 proviso, R.10(1)(2), R.13, O.6 R.17 proviso** verbatim?\n\n• ☐ Draw **Flowchart A (parties) + B (amendment) + pleading lifecycle** from memory?\n\n• ☐ Write **necessary/proper table + 2 tests + 3 examples each** in 8 min?\n\n• ☐ Write **Mulla 5 + Pollock + Steward/Weldon/Charan Das** in 8 min?\n\n• ☐ Summarise **Jai (business→proprietor, relate back), Ganesh (dissolution, bundle, Robinson/Dornan), Dalip (9, Rs.1000), BK (S.60(b), arrears+3000)** in 8 lines each?\n\n• ☐ Solve **tenant (refuse), Ghasita/ABC (allow, any stage + diligence)** with application para?\n\n#### 📖 SOURCES CITED\n\n*DU LB-302 (2025) pp.58–71 (Cases 11–14 full judgments); Bare Act O.1 Rr.1–13, O.6 Rr.1–2,7,16–18, O.30/S.69 context, S.21 Limitation; Universal Law Series (O.1 + O.6 R.17 Q&A, Cooper/Kisandas/Ganga Bai/Pirgonda/Heeralal); Takwani (Institution Ch.5, Pleadings Ch.6 — Throp, Steward/Weldon/Pollock, subsequent events); PYQ Q.2(a)/2019, Q.4(b)/2017, Q.2(a)/2018, Q.3/2020, S.21 block.* Bare quotes verified against workspace CPC text.\n\nDU LL.B LB-302 • Topics 9 & 10 Master Notes • Parties (O.1) • Amendment (O.6 R.17) • DU case material + Bare Act + Universal + Takwani + PYQ till 2023 • Study use • 9 Sept 2026\n🖨️ Print / Save PDF"
